+
+# Current Python recipes
+
+Install in an environment appropriate to the user's project:
+
+```sh
+python -m pip install jubarte-redlines
+python -c "import jubarte_redlines as j; print(j.__version__)"
+```
+
+Compare two existing files and write a new tracked DOCX:
+
+```python
+from pathlib import Path
+import jubarte_redlines as j
+
+original = Path("original.docx").read_bytes()
+modified = Path("modified.docx").read_bytes()
+redline = j.compare_documents(original, modified, author="Reviewer")
+with Path("redline.docx").open("xb") as target:
+    target.write(redline)
+for revision in j.get_revisions(redline):
+    print(revision["type"], revision["part"])
+```
+
+Render a DOCX with Word-style revision marks to a new PDF:
+
+```python
+from pathlib import Path
+from jubarte_redlines import docx_to_pdf
+
+pdf = docx_to_pdf(Path("redline.docx").read_bytes(), revisions="word")
+if not pdf.startswith(b"%PDF-"):
+    raise RuntimeError("renderer did not return a PDF")
+with Path("redline.pdf").open("xb") as target:
+    target.write(pdf)
+```
+
+Accept every tracked revision explicitly:
+
+```python
+from pathlib import Path
+from jubarte_redlines import accept_revisions
+
+clean = accept_revisions(Path("redline.docx").read_bytes())
+with Path("accepted.docx").open("xb") as target:
+    target.write(clean)
+```
+
+To reject every revision use `reject_revisions` with the same byte interface.
+This changes the selected document state; it is not a reversible edit history
+inside the resulting clean file. Keep the original separately.
+
+These recipes do not overwrite an existing output. Select a new destination on
+retry. Author/date defaults, font substitution and supported document structures
+follow the installed release; record its version when reporting a problem.
